+		<member name="rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/far_cascade_first" type="int" setter="" getter="" default="2">
+			First directional shadow cascade (0-based) affected by [member rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/far_cascade_update_interval]. Closer cascades are rendered every frame.
+		</member>
+		<member name="rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/far_cascade_margin" type="float" setter="" getter="" default="1.25">
+			Factor by which cached far cascades are enlarged, so they keep covering the view while the camera moves. Larger values allow more camera movement between updates at the cost of shadow resolution in those cascades.
+		</member>
+		<member name="rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/far_cascade_update_interval" type="int" setter="" getter="" default="1">
+			If greater than [code]1[/code], directional shadow cascades starting at [member rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/far_cascade_first] are rendered only every this many frames (staggered, so far cascades take turns) and reused in between. A cascade is rendered immediately if the light rotates, the shadow atlas changes, another viewport rendered directional shadows, or the camera moved or turned beyond what the cached cascade covers. Moving shadow casters in those cascades update with a delay of up to this many frames. Only supported by the Forward+ renderer.
+		</member>
 		<member name="rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/size" type="int" setter="" getter="" default="4096">
 			The directional shadow's size in pixels. Higher values will result in sharper shadows, at the cost of performance. The value is rounded up to the nearest power of 2.
 		</member>
